WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.370
Get running, get running

3
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.460
holding our flag high in the sky

4
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:18.060
Cross this endless sea with me and search for

5
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.810
a global miracle no one

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.940
has yet been able to find

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.960
With our hearts pounding,

8
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.710
we'll just charge ahead as we please, following

9
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.590
the footprints of those who pursue their dreams

10
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.390
No matter how stormy the night,

11
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.390
if we put our minds together,

12
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.540
we'll get through it

13
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.860
always

14
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.590
Get running, get running

15
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.550
holding our flag high in the sky

16
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.140
Even though there are tears

17
00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.580
we don't want anyone to see

18
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.520
Keep chasing, keep chasing

19
00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.520
the compass that leads to our dreams

20
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.230
always points straight ahead

21
00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.400
We can't stop here

22
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.490
Get running, get running,

23
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.540
head past everyone else

24
00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.120
So long as we don't run from it,

25
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.540
we can take hold of tomorrow

26
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.630
Keep chasing, keep chasing

27
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.510
everything we see in the moment,

28
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.930
we should record it all

29
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.430
in the blank slates of our minds

30
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.900
<b>The Hunter</b>

31
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.680
It's the mirage from earlier.

32
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.720
In the end, you've only got one body.

33
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.250
That's right. One of them is the real me.

34
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.180
The other four are illusions formed from reflections in the frigid air.

35
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.230
Illusions, you say?

36
00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:11.250
That sounds mysterious and lovely.

37
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.250
But when you think about it rationally,

38
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:17.240
illusions obviously don't have offensive power.

39
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.030
In other words, this is just an empty threat.

40
00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.240
That's right.

41
00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.330
So you turn defiant? You're not sweet, at all.

42
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.410
Thunder Charge!

43
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.270
Only one of these five is real.

44
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.270
So what?

45
00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:35.760
And...

46
00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.270
Thunder Ball!

47
00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.760
Only 20% of my attacks are real as well.
Why don't you try dodging them?

48
00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.510
Oh, shoot! I have to defend myself!
Which ones are real?!

49
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.660
Their power, on the other hand, is 100%.

50
00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.480
This is very different from the old Clima-Tact.

51
00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.410
A mere Thunder Ball attack
has this much power.

52
00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.830
With my next powerful attack, you're done.

53
00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.840
What kind of prediction is that? How cocky!

54
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.510
It's not a prediction. It's a forecast.

55
00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.900
I control both the humidity and temperature.

56
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.640
The weather in this room belongs to me!

57
00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.230
What's the big deal with
controlling the weather?

58
00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.980
The Six Powers are techniques
that exceed human abilities.

59
00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.100
How insolent!

60
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.400
That wasn't the real one!

61
00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.150
Today, the chance of finding the real me is still 20%.

62
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.680
While atmospheric pressure is stable, today's skies show signs...

63
00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.460
of a stationary front of small, dark clouds and violent winds.

64
00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.550
Given time, a clap of thunder should signal the lightning that will pierce your chest.

65
00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:02.260
Beware of cardiac arrest!

66
00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.430
Dark Cloud Tempo!

67
00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.240
If this is lightning, I showed you earlier that I can guard myself.

68
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.640
As long as I'm being careful...

69
00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:14.650
The flaw in that technique is that
you can't move around while using it.

70
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:23.420
You sure take me lightly. Are you
telling me to break it with an attack?!

71
00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:24.540
Then...

72
00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.370
Soap Sheep!

73
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.350
I don't have to know which one is the real one.

74
00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:33.460
I'll swallow everything with a
big wave of Relaxing Bubbles.

75
00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.330
Sheep Cloud!

76
00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.500
Tidal Wave!

77
00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.260
I'll be a goner if I get hit by that.

78
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.180
The one on the floor after I
swallow everything is the real one.

79
00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.680
That's not gonna happen!

80
00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.390
Cyclone Tempo!

81
00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.630
She used wind to blow the bubbles away!

82
00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.440
But it looks like the one who got
through it is the real one, huh?

83
00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.740
Finger Pistol!

84
00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.440
Oh? I thought it was another illusion.

85
00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.150
I won't let you get away again.

86
00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:35.140
I'll just riddle your body with holes.

87
00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.110
You've already forgotten it, haven't you?

88
00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:47.030
You should pay attention to
a navigator's weather forecast.

89
00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.170
A thunderbolt will surge out...

90
00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.750
from the dark clouds to the Clima-Tact!

91
00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:04.510
Come on!

92
00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.150
The clouds from earlier!

93
00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.140
Thunder Lance Tempo!

94
00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.230
No matter how strong you are,

95
00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.940
my forecasts are never wrong.

96
00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.610
My friends are waiting. I'll be taking your key.

97
00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.540
Deer-gorilla! Where'd you go?!

98
00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.760
What? Franky! What are you doing there?!

99
00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:02.950
Oh, hey, lady.

100
00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.770
That monster deer-gorilla in
your group came here, didn't he?

101
00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.980
Deer... You mean Chopper?

102
00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:11.990
Yeah, that deer-gorilla.

103
00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:16.290
Yeah, he did. What's the deal?
What happened to him?

104
00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.220
How should I know?! That was my question!

105
00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.960
Isn't he someone who can transform like that?

106
00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.170
How would I know?!
I've never seen him in that form.

107
00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:30.010
I see. I thought you guys
might know how to deal with that.

108
00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.840
Then, I guess I'll just kill him.

109
00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.440
If you say that again, I'm gonna kill you.

110
00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.390
I-I'll never say it again. Ever again.

111
00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:47.560
By the way, you're not bad yourself.
You took this woman down?

112
00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.900
Her key is important: the No. 2 key.

113
00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:54.320
The key! Hold on a sec. I was just looking for it.

114
00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.780
Key! Key! Where'd you hide it?

115
00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:00.040
Yow! Nice scandalous behavior!

116
00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.170
What the hell is this monster?!

117
00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:07.620
Was there someone else with a zoan-type ability?!

118
00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.970
Does that mean that this
guy's also part of CP9?!

119
00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.470
Come to think of it, I feel
like I've seen him before.

120
00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.050
Ch-Chopper?!

121
00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.690
What're you doing, Chopper?! It's us!

122
00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.600
Ahh! Stop it!

123
00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:31.240
Hey, is that really Chopper?!
How come he doesn't recognize us?!

124
00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:36.420
I don't know, but it must be Chopper!
Who else has those antlers and wears that hat?!

125
00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:39.510
So, where's our only chance? Where's the No. 2 key?!

126
00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.650
Who knows? This is it! We're gonna die.

127
00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:45.330
But something is wrong.

128
00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.840
Isn't he the one who looks
like he is about to die?

129
00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.860
It seems as if his life force is rapidly fading.

130
00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.850
Wh-Wh-What does that mean?

131
00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:00.430
It may be that him staying in that form
uses up too much energy or something.

132
00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:04.070
What the hell?! What do we do
about him and the other two?!

133
00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:07.610
Hey, what happened to the key?
Where's the No. 2 key?!

134
00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.890
I don't know what happened,

135
00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:13.850
but he must've fought incredibly hard...

136
00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.910
So hard that he transformed into that.

137
00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.120
No. 2...

138
00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.750
That's quite the interruption. What's that monster?

139
00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.090
The buster call is imminent.

140
00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:32.710
Of course he'd interrupt us.
It seems like he's one of those pirates.

141
00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.070
Anything that gets in our way...

142
00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.820
Should be eliminated.

143
00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.080
Although he's insignificant...

144
00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.850
We've got more prey.

145
00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:46.510
Dammit! They're gonna attack Chopper!

146
00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:49.080
Straighten your back,
named blade Nose Storm.

147
00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.770
H-Hey! What're you gonna do?!

148
00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.220
36-Pound Phoenix!

149
00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.070
You bastard!

150
00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.190
Step aside, you guys!

151
00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.280
– Huh?
– That guy...!

152
00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.620
Franky! What're you trying to do?!

153
00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.870
This is one of our...

154
00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.960
I know! Just be quiet.

155
00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.830
This is the only way that I
can think of to deal with him.

156
00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.920
Everyone with devil fruit powers has a weakness.

157
00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.870
I'll push him out to sea.

158
00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.430
I'll go easy, so bear with me!

159
00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.910
Coup de...

160
00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.770
Vent!

161
00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.840
You bastard, Franky! That's reckless!

162
00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.330
What're you doing to our friend?!

163
00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:47.180
Don't worry. He discussed
this with me beforehand.

164
00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.290
What?

165
00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:05.290
What're they doing, attacking their own?

166
00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.140
They sure do make a big fuss.

167
00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:18.440
So you're finally free?

168
00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.410
You'd better stop smiling and start regretting.

169
00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.870
Never again...

170
00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:29.950
will you get a chance to kill me like the one you just had,

171
00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.080
World Government!

172
00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.460
Battleships are preparing their attack!

173
00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.840
Get off of Enies Lobby!

174
00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.720
They're gonna start firing cannons!

175
00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:40.260
Everyone, get off of the island!

176
00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.170
We'll get dragged into the buster call!

177
00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.810
We'll die if we stay here!

178
00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.790
Stop, Nico Robin!

179
00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.800
Even if you go back the way we came,
all you'll find are the corpses of pirates!

180
00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.450
Enough already.

181
00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.880
Teach her a lesson, Funkfreed!

182
00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.420
Luffy is just ahead.

183
00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.810
Don't hit her vital spots, got that?

184
00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.460
Ivory...

185
00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:24.820
Dart!

186
00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:43.590
I won't let you escape, you dumb woman!

187
00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:45.200
Don't underestimate me!

188
00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:49.990
Now, let's go through the
door to our dreams.

189
00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.780
He's back to normal.

190
00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.220
He'd better not be dead.

191
00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.140
I didn't expect that even his friends
wouldn't know how to handle that.

192
00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:11.440
Don't you wanna save Nico Robin?!

193
00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.420
I do!

194
00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:18.560
Well, anyway, the fact remains
that he took out a member of CP9.

195
00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.730
In consideration of your friends who
defended you even after you turned...

196
00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:27.240
into such a terrible form,
I'll forgive you for attacking me.

197
00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.270
We'd better hurry.

198
00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:38.600
But... even if I hurry, I still don't know
how to get to the Gates of Justice.

199
00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.280
We'll be your guides!

200
00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.040
Little ones!

201
00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.590
I found Franky!

202
00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:51.930
What?! You guys know where the
passage to the Gates of Justice is?!

203
00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:55.830
Yep, we do! We're here to be guides!

204
00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:59.150
Grandma's over there, too.

205
00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.170
Tell me where it is right away!

206
00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:04.390
And I'll give you and old hag Kokoro
instructions as to what you should do!

207
00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.260
Roger.

208
00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:12.370
He's unconscious, but seems to be okay.

209
00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:17.660
Oh, no! I have to bring the keys
to Nico Robin as soon as possible!

210
00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.670
You guys bring that deer when you come in a bit!

211
00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:24.310
– Okay.
– Got it! Go, Franky!

212
00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:33.310
So, we have no choice but
to do that to stop Chopper.

213
00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:38.350
And then, after that, take these
No. 3 and No. 4 keys and hurry to Robin.

214
00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.770
One of them might unlock her handcuffs.

215
00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:45.700
If so, call me using this portable
transponder snail that secretary had.

216
00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.310
Okay.

217
00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.990
Leave freeing Zoro and Noseking to me.

218
00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.600
That's fine, but what will we do after that?

219
00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:59.480
We've come this far, but even if
we're able to rescue Nico Robin,

220
00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:03.840
there's still no bridge between this tower
and Enies Lobby. So we can't go back.

221
00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:05.350
Yeah.

222
00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:07.350
Now that a buster call has been sounded,

223
00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:10.470
we don't have time to go back
the way we came in the first place.

224
00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:11.140
So?

225
00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.300
So there's no question about it, right?

226
00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.700
Behind us is a deadly waterfall.
Ahead of us is a mysterious path.

227
00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:20.810
Which would you pick?

228
00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.560
Well, I guess that ahead is the only way.

229
00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:26.250
Then, when we're done with
what we have to do here,

230
00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.360
we'll all gather at the Gates of Justice!

231
00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.360
As for what's after that, just leave it to...

232
00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.020
– To you?!
– To luck!

233
00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:33.620
Luck?!

234
00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:42.030
We've...

235
00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:43.750
Wasted quite a bit of time.

236
00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.960
Damn straight!

237
00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:50.170
I can't believe you guys have been
acting so dumb during an ordeal like this!

238
00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.130
That's because this guy was doing stupid stuff.

239
00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:56.310
You both are brainless!
Hurry up and get their keys already!

240
00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.560
Tempest Kick:

241
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:00.900
Wire!

242
00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:05.790
That's just as I instructed. Nice job, Zoro-kun!

243
00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.260
Fight! Zoro!

244
00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:09.360
You guys fight, too!

245
00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.950
That long neck of yours...

246
00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.450
You'd better hope it doesn't
become your weak point.

247
00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.450
No need to worry about that.

248
00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.500
I gained muscles that are strong enough
to give me full control of my neck.

249
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.790
And they've got the power of bullets, too!

250
00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.300
Nose Pistol!

251
00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.140
Wh-What the heck?

252
00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.350
How can we feel this much impact from here?!

253
00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.870
His nose made a square-shaped hole in that rock!

254
00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.690
That nose is more amazing than Sogepp's!

255
00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:02.140
Wh-Wh-Who're you calling Sogepp?!

256
00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.700
And don't make needless
comparisons like that!

257
00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:05.610
Well, at any rate...

258
00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:09.250
Kaku's gotten quite
proficient at using his powers.

259
00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:15.350
W-Wolf! I-I'm your adversary!

260
00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:18.050
Hm? Don't get so worked up.

261
00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:21.520
You guys wanna save your friend, right?

262
00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.890
Th-That's right! I'll take your key!

263
00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:26.980
Hm?

264
00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:29.390
Huh?

265
00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.710
Hurry up and take it to her.

266
00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.120
What?

267
00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:36.350
Go save Nico Robin.

268
00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:38.620
Wh-What on earth are you...

269
00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:45.210
To be honest, I don't wanna
kill people. I hate blood.

270
00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.290
Hm?

271
00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:49.920
Th-Then, I'll just...

272
00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.960
take the key and...

273
00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:55.350
No! Watch out!

274
00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.720
Ten Finger Pistol!

275
00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:04.220
Don't let your guard down.

276
00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:08.270
I'm a wolf. I put people off
their guard then go for the throat.

277
00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.120
Usopp!

278
00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:27.870
D-Dammit! What am I doing?

279
00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.040
What an unbelievable masked idiot!

280
00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.330
Why don't you just run
around like you did earlier?

281
00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:37.510
You're fast as lightning
when you're running away.

282
00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.330
Stop mocking me.

283
00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.180
Huh?

284
00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:46.470
We no longer have that kind of time.

285
00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.690
Advanced Kabuto!

286
00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:52.020
Lethal Sunflower Star!

287
00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.320
Oh?

288
00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.080
Oh, I see. Fireworks, huh?

289
00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:09.700
Usopp!

290
00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:11.000
Moon Walk!

291
00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.180
Stop it!

292
00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:43.360
As I promised, your death will be instantaneous and without pain.

293
00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:47.040
Too bad. If you'd stayed connected with
that shepherd and had him protect you,

294
00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.910
you would've been okay.

295
00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:53.880
You see what happens when a
lamb wanders off all by himself?

296
00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:57.340
He gets eaten by a scary wolf.

297
00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.780
Now, this is it for you!

298
00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:05.430
Hey, stop it, wolf! You bastard!

299
00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.560
Don't kill him! Please! We don't need your key!

300
00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.960
You fool! You'll die next!

301
00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.480
Tempest Kick!

302
00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:19.860
Dammit!

303
00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.490
Now, die!

304
00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:30.340
Usopp!

305
00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.980
Who the hell are you?!

306
00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.220
The hunter.
